# N64 Decompilation Process

## Initial Setup

### Clean and Build
<pre>
./configure --clean legoracers.e.z64
ninja check
</pre>

### Configure Splat
When setting up a new file for decompilation:

1. Locate the file segments in splat configuration
2. Convert segment types:
   - Change "asm" segments to "cpp" 
   - Change "rdata" segments to ".rdata"
   - Leave "data" segments unchanged

Example:
<pre>
# Before:
segment.add_segment(0x33170, "rdata", "stage2/040")
segment.add_segment(0x39CC0, "asm", "stage2/040")
segment.add_segment(0x79AF0, "data", "stage2/040")

# After:
segment.add_segment(0x33170, ".rdata", "stage2/040")
segment.add_segment(0x39CC0, "cpp", "stage2/040")
segment.add_segment(0x79AF0, "data", "stage2/040")
</pre>

After making these changes:
1. Run `./configure --clean legoracers.e.z64` again
2. Verify new C file was created (e.g. src/stage2/040.cpp)
3. Run `ninja check` to verify build still matches
